---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { href, site } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture | Rintu Chowdory"
  description="How the portfolio is put together: an Astro site on GitHub Pages, a FastAPI service on Vercel, GitHub Actions shipping both, and one endpoint that reports the real pipeline."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-indigo-300">Architecture</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl">How the pieces fit</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-400">
      Two repositories, one delivery path. The site is static, the API is serverless and the CI
      numbers on the dashboard come from the same GitHub Actions runs that shipped this page.
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- DIAGRAM -->
  <section class="glass-panel mt-8 overflow-hidden p-4 sm:p-6">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-300">Request and build path</h2>
      <a class="text-xs text-indigo-300 hover:text-white" href={href("/case-study")}>Why it is built this way</a>
    </div>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 420" class="mt-5 w-full" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: a push runs GitHub Actions, which publishes a container image to GHCR and a static build to GitHub Pages; the browser loads the site and calls a FastAPI service on Vercel, which reads workflow runs from the GitHub API.">
      <defs>
        <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#5b6b85" />
        </marker>
        <linearGradient id="halo" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#7c6cff" stop-opacity="0.18" />
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#38bdf8" stop-opacity="0.06" />
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>

      <!-- column labels -->
      <text x="40" y="26" fill="#7b8aa3" font-size="11" letter-spacing="2">BUILD</text>
      <text x="420" y="26" fill="#7b8aa3" font-size="11" letter-spacing="2">ARTEFACTS</text>
      <text x="760" y="26" fill="#7b8aa3" font-size="11" letter-spacing="2">RUNTIME</text>

      <!-- build column -->
      <rect x="40" y="44" width="250" height="72" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="58" y="72" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">git push to main</text>
      <text x="58" y="94" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">rintuchowdory / devops-portfolio-*</text>

      <rect x="40" y="140" width="250" height="120" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="58" y="168" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">GitHub Actions</text>
      <text x="58" y="190" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">ci.yml · ruff, pytest 3.11-3.13</text>
      <text x="58" y="209" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">build, Trivy scan, smoke test</text>
      <text x="58" y="228" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">deploy.yml · Pages build</text>
      <text x="58" y="247" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">fail closed on a missing page</text>

      <rect x="40" y="284" width="250" height="76" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="58" y="312" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">GHCR</text>
      <text x="58" y="334" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">tagged image, provenance, SBOM</text>

      <!-- artefact column -->
      <rect x="400" y="120" width="240" height="86" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="418" y="148" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">GitHub Pages</text>
      <text x="418" y="170" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">10 static pages, no server</text>
      <text x="418" y="189" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">headline numbers built in</text>

      <rect x="400" y="240" width="240" height="86" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="418" y="268" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">Vercel · FastAPI</text>
      <text x="418" y="290" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">/health · /metrics · /api/v1</text>
      <text x="418" y="309" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">serverless, JSON errors</text>

      <!-- runtime column -->
      <rect x="740" y="120" width="220" height="76" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="758" y="148" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">Browser</text>
      <text x="758" y="170" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">polls every 4-5 s</text>

      <rect x="740" y="230" width="220" height="96" rx="10" fill="url(#halo)" stroke="#2a3550" />
      <text x="758" y="258" fill="#e7eefc" font-size="15" font-weight="600">GitHub API</text>
      <text x="758" y="280" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">real workflow runs</text>
      <text x="758" y="299" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">60 s cache per worker</text>
      <text x="758" y="318" fill="#8fa1bb" font-size="12">falls back to demo data</text>

      <!-- arrows -->
      <!-- push -> CI -->
      <path d="M 165 120 L 165 136" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- CI -> image registry -->
      <path d="M 165 264 L 165 280" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- CI -> static build -->
      <path d="M 290 190 L 355 190 L 355 163 L 393 163" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- CI -> api deployment -->
      <path d="M 290 236 L 340 236 L 340 283 L 393 283" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- static build -> browser -->
      <path d="M 640 163 L 737 158" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- browser -> api -->
      <path d="M 850 196 L 850 300 L 648 300" fill="none" stroke="#5b6b85" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <!-- api reads github runs -->
      <path d="M 850 326 L 850 356 L 520 356 L 520 330" fill="none" stroke="#22c55e" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

      <text x="356" y="152" fill="#5b6b85" font-size="11">static build</text>
      <text x="345" y="276" fill="#5b6b85" font-size="11">deploy</text>
      <text x="656" y="140" fill="#5b6b85" font-size="11">GET /</text>
      <text x="676" y="318" fill="#5b6b85" font-size="11">fetch /api/v1 (CORS)</text>
      <text x="540" y="374" fill="#22c55e" font-size="11">real workflow runs, read back onto the dashboard</text>
    </svg>
  </section>

  <!-- BUILD PATH -->
  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="glass-panel p-5 sm:p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Build path</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">1.</span> A push to <span class="mono text-slate-200">main</span> starts two workflows: <span class="mono text-slate-200">ci.yml</span> in the microservice and <span class="mono text-slate-200">deploy.yml</span> in this site.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">2.</span> CI lints, then runs the suite on Python 3.11, 3.12 and 3.13, so a version-specific break cannot hide behind a green matrix.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">3.</span> The image is built, scanned and smoke tested by actually starting it and hitting <span class="mono text-slate-200">/health</span>, then pushed to GHCR with provenance and an SBOM.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">4.</span> The site build fetches the API while rendering, so the headline numbers are baked into static HTML. The deploy job fails if a page or the CSS bundle is missing.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>

    <article class="glass-panel p-5 sm:p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Runtime path</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">1.</span> The browser loads static HTML from Pages. Nothing is server-rendered, so the first paint never waits for the API.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">2.</span> Two small inline scripts poll <span class="mono text-slate-200">/health</span>, the summary, the log feed and the pipeline list every few seconds.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">3.</span> The API reads workflow runs from the GitHub API through a 60 second cache, so a busy dashboard costs GitHub one request a minute rather than one per refresh.</li>
        <li><span class="mono text-indigo-300">4.</span> Every fetch fails soft. Cold start, rate limit or an outage leaves the last numbers in place instead of an empty panel.</li>
      </ol>
    </article>
  </section>

  <!-- TRADE OFFS -->
  <section class="mt-10">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Trade-offs I made on purpose</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="table table-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Decision</th>
            <th>Why</th>
            <th>What it costs</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-slate-400">
          <tr>
            <td class="text-slate-200">Static site plus a separate API</td>
            <td>Free hosting, nothing to patch on a server, and the split is the actual thing a DevOps portfolio should demonstrate.</td>
            <td>Two deploys, and a CORS allow-list to keep honest.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-slate-200">Serverless instead of a container platform</td>
            <td>The account's free container slots were full, and a running URL beats a YAML file nobody executes.</td>
            <td>Cold starts of about half a second, and no long-lived background workers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-slate-200">Real CI data, demo telemetry elsewhere</td>
            <td>Fabricated dashboards are the fastest way to lose a technical reader. Pipelines are the one thing I can source truthfully for free.</td>
            <td>The response has to say which is which, so <span class="mono">source</span> is part of the contract.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-slate-200">Cache in front of the GitHub API</td>
            <td>5000 requests an hour is plenty, but not if every browser refresh spends one.</td>
            <td>Up to a minute of staleness, which is invisible next to a build that takes 80 seconds.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="text-slate-200">No Kubernetes, yet</td>
            <td>A cluster I cannot afford would be a screenshot, not a skill.</td>
            <td>The Kubernetes panel on the dashboard is clearly demo data until there is a real cluster behind it.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a class="btn border-0 bg-white text-[#05080f] hover:bg-slate-200" href={href("/case-study")}>Read the case study</a>
    <a class="btn btn-outline border-white/25 text-white hover:bg-white/10" href={href("/dashboard")}>Open the dashboard</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost text-slate-300" href={site.repoMicroservice} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Microservice source</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
